{%- comment -%}
  Product card for a one-of-a-kind salvage part.
  Accepts: card_product (product), eager (boolean, default false)

  Pass eager: true for the one image likely to be the largest thing in the first
  screenful — the LCP candidate — and leave every other card lazy. This used to take a
  `lazy` boolean and the two grid callers passed `lazy: forloop.first`, which inverted
  it: the first card, the one above the fold, was the only lazy image on the page, and
  all twenty-three below it loaded eagerly. Naming the flag after the exception rather
  than the default makes that mistake harder to make again.

  Every part is a single unit with its own Part ID, so the card leads with
  what a yard buyer actually compares: part type, the vehicle it came off,
  grade, and whether a real photo exists.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign p = card_product
  assign img = p.featured_media
  assign fit = settings.card_image_fit | default: 'cover'
  assign loading = 'lazy'
  if eager
    assign loading = 'eager'
  endif

  comment
    Whether the featured image is really this listing's — see 'photo-source'. 'none' means
    no photo, or one stray frame belonging to neither this part nor a donor shoot; the card
    then shows the placeholder, not that frame.
  endcomment
  capture card_photos
    render 'photo-source', product: p
  endcapture
-%}

{%- if p == blank -%}
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card__media"><div class="card__placeholder">{% render 'icon', name: 'photo' %}</div></div>
    <div class="card__body">
      <p class="card__title">{{ 'general.onboarding' | default: 'Example part' }}</p>
      <div class="card__foot"><span class="price">$0.00</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
{%- else -%}
  <article class="card" data-product-id="{{ p.id }}">
    <div class="card__media{% if fit == 'contain' %} card__media--contain{% endif %}">
      {%- if img and card_photos != 'none' -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Build the alt text first, for the reason header.liquid records: a `|` inside a
          filter argument does not belong to that argument. Liquid ends image_tag's argument
          list there and chains the rest onto image_tag's own *output*, so this read as
          `escape(default(image_tag(...), p.title))` — escaping the rendered <img> tag into
          visible markup instead of escaping the alt string.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign card_alt = img.alt | default: p.title | escape -%}
        {{ img | image_url: width: 800 | image_tag:
             widths: '200,300,400,600,800',
             sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 300px, 45vw',
             loading: loading,
             alt: card_alt }}
      {%- else -%}
        <div class="card__placeholder">{% render 'icon', name: 'photo' %}</div>
      {%- endif -%}

      <div class="card__flags">
        {%- comment -%}
          The card's compact shipping badge. It used to be an if/elsif chain here, reading
          "anything that isn't free is freight" — which was true while freight was the only
          rate, and quietly wrong the day a paid ground group was added. 'shipping-group'
          owns the wording and the rates for every shape, this one included.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {% render 'shipping-group', product: p, style: 'card' %}
        {%- unless p.available -%}
          <span class="badge badge--sold">Sold</span>
        {%- endunless -%}
        {%- if settings.card_show_grade -%}
          {%- assign grade = p.metafields.abm.grade | default: p.metafields.custom.grade -%}
          {%- if grade != blank -%}
            <span class="badge badge--green">Grade {{ grade }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        No photo count and no donor caption on the card. Both were removed deliberately:
        the count told a shopper nothing they could not see by looking, and carrying it on
        every card made the grid read as cluttered and over-explained.

        The disclosure this replaced is NOT lost — 'main-product' states it in full ("These
        photos are of the donor vehicle this part was removed from — not the part itself"),
        which is the surface a shopper has to pass before they can buy. If a pre-click
        caveat is ever wanted back, add it here, not as a count.
      {%- endcomment -%}
    </div>

    <div class="card__body">
      {%- if settings.card_show_type and p.type != blank -%}
        <span class="card__type">{{ p.type }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}

      <h3 class="card__title">
        <a href="{{ p.url }}">{{ p.title }}</a>
      </h3>

      <div class="card__meta">
        {% render 'shipping-group', product: p, style: 'line' %}
      </div>

      <div class="card__meta">
        {%- if settings.card_show_sku and p.selected_or_first_available_variant.sku != blank -%}
          <span>Part&nbsp;ID&nbsp;<b>{{ p.selected_or_first_available_variant.sku }}</b></span>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- assign miles = p.metafields.abm.mileage -%}
        {%- comment -%} Same comma formatting the product page's Mileage row uses. {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if miles != blank -%}<span>{%- render 'count-with-delimiters', count: miles -%}&nbsp;mi</span>{%- endif -%}
      </div>

      <div class="card__foot">
        {% render 'price', product: p %}
        {%- if p.available -%}
          <span class="small" style="color:var(--green-dark);font-weight:700;">In stock</span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
{%- endif -%}
